## Format the Logical Volume

### Command

```bash id="ph5c2p"
mkfs.ext4 /dev/tws-vg/tws-lv
```

### What I Observed

The logical volume was formatted with the `ext4` filesystem.

### ⚠️ Important Warning

`mkfs` creates a new filesystem and can destroy existing data on the target device.

Before formatting a production or existing device, always verify the device carefully:

```bash
lsblk
```

```bash
df -h
```

Formatting should only be performed when the device is intended to be newly formatted or its existing data can safely be erased.

