# Task 4 – Extend the Logical Volume

## Extend the Logical Volume

### Command

```bash id="6w8j0c"
lvextend -L +2G /dev/tws-vg/tws-lv
```

### What I Observed

Increased the logical volume size by **2 GB**.

### Important Concept

`lvextend` increases the size of the **logical volume**.

The filesystem inside the LV may still need to be resized separately.

```text
LV size increased
       ↓
Filesystem may still have old size
       ↓
Resize filesystem
```

---

## Verify the Logical Volume

```bash id="1o8dlp"
lsblk
```

### What I Observed

Checked the logical volume size after extending it.

---

## Check Filesystem Size

```bash id="6c6v0x"
