# Important LVM Concept

The resize process can be understood as:

```text
Before

Physical Disk
     ↓
Physical Volume
     ↓
Volume Group
     ↓
Logical Volume
     ↓
Filesystem
     ↓
Mount Point


After lvextend

Physical Disk
     ↓
Physical Volume
     ↓
Volume Group
     ↓
Larger Logical Volume
     ↓
Filesystem
     ↓
Mount Point
```

### Key Point

> Increasing the LV size and increasing the filesystem size are related but separate operations.

Using:

```bash id="rd7t2h"
lvextend -r -L +2G /dev/tws-vg/tws-lv
```

allows the logical volume and filesystem to be resized together.

