# What I Learned

### 1. `lsblk`

`lsblk` helps understand the disk, partition, filesystem, and logical-volume structure of a Linux system.

### 2. `df -h`

`df -h` shows filesystem capacity, used space, and available space.

### 3. `mount`

`mount` connects a filesystem or block device to a directory in the Linux filesystem.

### 4. `lvextend`

`lvextend` increases the size of an LVM logical volume.

### 5. `lvextend -r`

Using `-r` allows the filesystem to be resized along with the logical volume.

### 6. `mkfs`

`mkfs` creates a filesystem on a block device.

> Always verify the target device before using `mkfs`, because formatting can destroy existing data.

