# Real-World DevOps Connection

LVM is useful when a Linux server starts running out of disk space.

For example:

```text
Application
     ↓
/opt/app
     ↓
Filesystem
     ↓
Logical Volume
     ↓
Volume Group
```

If more capacity is available in the volume group, the logical volume can be extended without replacing the entire filesystem.

A typical investigation may start with:

```bash
df -h
```

Then:

```bash
lsblk
```

```bash
pvs
```

```bash
vgs
```

```bash
lvs
```

This helps determine where additional storage is available and which layer needs to be extended.

